1
00:00:10,714 --> 00:00:16,714
Burlesque is a drama film directed by Dominic Deacon.

2
00:00:21,428 --> 00:00:27,428
Frank Bannister is about to have a very long night.

3
00:00:32,142 --> 00:00:38,142
A writer of violent horror stories, Frank is alone,
depressed and one step from full blown alcoholism.

4
00:00:42,857 --> 00:00:48,857
Late one dark and stormy night his quiet hermit existence is disturbed
when two eccentric exotic dancers arrive on his doorstep.

5
00:00:53,571 --> 00:00:59,571
Alternatively seductive and sinister the beautiful women
promise to make all Frank's dreams come true.

6
00:01:04,285 --> 00:01:10,285
They prove to be as good as their word.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Only problem is, Frank is a man with very dark dreams indeed.

8
00:01:25,714 --> 00:01:31,714
Frank Bannister, played by Haydn Evans.

9
00:01:36,428 --> 00:01:42,428
Veronica, played by Christina Hallett.

10
00:01:47,142 --> 00:01:53,142
Tammy, played by Poppy Cherry.

11
00:01:57,857 --> 00:02:03,857
Fiona, played by Virginia Bowers.

12
00:02:08,571 --> 00:02:14,571
Richard, played by Dennis Kreusler.

13
00:02:19,285 --> 00:02:25,285
Burlesque is a 2010 American backstage musical film
written and directed by Steven Antin.

14
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
It stars Cher, Christina Aguilera in her film debut, Kristen Bell, Cam Gigandet, Stanley Tucci, Julianne
Hough, Alan Cumming, and Peter Gallagher, and features cameos from Dianna Agron and James Brolin.

15
00:02:40,714 --> 00:02:46,714
The film tells the story of Ali (Aguilera), an aspiring singer who leaves her small hometown for Los
Angeles, where she becomes a dancer at a struggling burlesque lounge owned by Tess (Cher).

16
00:02:51,428 --> 00:02:57,428
After a performance is sabotaged by her rival, Nikki (Bell), Ali sings the song herself,
impressing Tess and leading to her becoming the main attraction of the lounge.

17
00:03:02,142 --> 00:03:08,142
Burlesque marks Aguilera's first leading role, as well as Cher's first
musical performance on screen since 1967's Good Times.

18
00:03:12,857 --> 00:03:18,857
Filming for Burlesque took place in California from November 2009 to March 2010.

19
00:03:23,571 --> 00:03:29,571
It was released in the United States on November 24, 2010, by Screen Gems.

20
00:03:34,285 --> 00:03:40,285
Its jazz-inspired soundtrack was released ahead of the film's release
on November 19, 2010, by RCA Records and Screen Gems.

21
00:03:44,999 --> 00:03:50,999
Aguilera and Cher both contributed to the album.

22
00:03:55,714 --> 00:04:01,714
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the cast's
performance and the soundtrack but criticized the writing.

23
00:04:06,428 --> 00:04:12,428
Burlesque did modestly at the box office, grossing $91 million worldwide and
earning an additional $42 million in domestic video sales.

24
00:04:17,142 --> 00:04:23,142
The film was nominated for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy at the 68th Golden Globe Awards, where Cher's
performance of "You Haven't Seen the Last of Me", written by Diane Warren, won for Best Original Song.

25
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:33,857
The soundtrack was nominated for Best Compilation Soundtrack
for Visual Media in the 54th Grammy Awards.

26
00:04:38,571 --> 00:04:44,571
A stage musical adaptation of the film premiered in June 2024.

27
00:04:49,285 --> 00:04:55,285
The tone is dark and emotional.
